  "description": "A points and rewards engine for ASP.NET Core and EF Core. Your app reports what users do; rules decide the points; a ledger keeps every change; users spend points on rewards your business funds.\n\nWhat you get:\n• Points engine: rules per event type with JSON conditions, per-day limits, and daily and weekly caps. Platform defaults, with per-tenant overrides.\n• Pays once: an event type and reference credit at most once per user, enforced by a unique index, so retries and duplicate messages never double-pay.\n• Ledger-based wallets: every earn, spend, refund, expiry and adjustment is a row. Balances use optimistic concurrency, so two spends can't overdraw.\n• Rewards: a catalogue with stock and availability windows, redemption codes to show at the desk, staff fulfilment or instant rewards, cancel with refund, and automatic expiry of uncollected rewards.\n• Points expiry, staff adjustments with a note, levels from lifetime points, and programme stats.\n\nExample: an online learning platform\nEach school is a tenant. Learners earn 50 points per lesson (up to 3 a day), 20 for a quiz scored 80 or more, and 150 for a 7-day streak. Northbridge Academy adds 10 points for lessons before 7am in its own time zone and caps earning at 300 a day. A learner spends 500 points on a 1:1 tutor session and reads the code RW-7K3QX9 to staff. If staff cancel it, the points come back once, and the slot returns to stock.\n\nCall modelBuilder.ApplyGamificationModel() and services.AddGamification<AppDb>(). Targets .NET 8 (EF Core 8) and .NET 10 (EF Core 10). Works with any EF Core relational provider.",
